Roast.pet Frontier Stack =E2=80=94 NO MATERIAL STACK DELTA

Fresh scan across GitHub, Hugging Face, recent model/API releases,
video/avatar/lip-sync/TTS, segmentation/background removal, WebXR/AR,
fal/Replicate-style hosting, Etsy/Shopify, POD and workflow surfaces found
no newly released or materially improved Roast.pet-specific item that
clears the inclusion bar this hour.

I explicitly excluded mature unchanged tools, marketing/listicle
recirculation, and items already captured in earlier scans (including
H3/VDN-H3, LongCat, P-Video-2-Pro, ModelRunner, Knockout/BiRefNet and
Falcon 2).
Current top 5 stack changes to test now

   1. Fixed hard-pet benchmark: H3 Max vs LongCat vs Wan using identical
   selected audio.
   2. P-Video-2-Pro Speed as cheap best-of-N draft/motion generation, with
   premium escalation only after QC.
   3. Local pet cutout =E2=86=92 automated fur/edge QC =E2=86=92 hosted fal=
lback, producing
   one canonical transparent PetAsset.
   4. Generate multiple cheap TTS performances and rank comedy/timing
   before paying for video animation.
   5. Unified audiovisual QC gate that retries cheap renders and escalates
   only failures/premium orders.

Cheapest meaningful capability improvement

Still local/browser segmentation at effectively $0 marginal inference,
followed by selecting TTS before video so failed comedic takes never incur
animation cost.
Biggest capability shock this hour

None. Search results were dominated by unchanged tools, recirculated
comparisons, and previously captured releases rather than a verified new
capability.
Concrete stack simplification

Keep the stable pipeline provider-neutral:

PetPrep =E2=86=92 PetAsset =E2=86=92 RoastSpec =E2=86=92 VoiceRenderer(N ta=
kes) =E2=86=92 ComedyRanker =E2=86=92
VideoRenderer =E2=86=92 AV-QC =E2=86=92 Captions/QR/POD

Do not add another vendor integration until a candidate beats an existing
component on the fixed regression corpus for quality, usable-render rate,
latency, or cost.

